  "answer": "To reduce the risk that function-approximation errors and mandatory random exploration in reinforcement learning cause an agent to repeatedly select actions leading to catastrophic or severe penalties, researchers have proposed integrating safe exploration constraints during training (https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/kj37Hzb2MsALwLqWt/alignment-research-exercises). The proposed mechanism involves modifying the learning objective or policy to respect safety constraints by incorporating a safety-critic or action-mask, penalizing catastrophic states through penalized updates, and adjusting exploration to shield or avoid actions whose worst-case value is below a given threshold (https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/kj37Hzb2MsALwLqWt/alignment-research-exercises)."
